<BaseLayout title="Our Story | House of Agape" description="Learn about the vision, mission, and founder behind House of Agape.">
  <section class="page-hero section-shell"><p class="eyebrow">Our story</p><h1>Love that makes room for healing.</h1><p class="lede">House of Agape is rooted in the belief that every person deserves a safe, compassionate place to pause, care for themselves, and begin again.</p></section>
  <section class="section-shell mission-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">Mission</p><h2>Practical care for life’s journey.</h2><p>Our mission is to provide products and experiences that help people navigate life with love through a holistic approach to self-care, practical tools, approachable faith-informed teaching, and supportive resources for wellness.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Vision</p><h2>Healing the world, one person at a time.</h2><p>We envision a welcoming self-love and healing ministry that creates room for outreach, programs, services, and resources that help people feel supported and seen.</p></article></section>
  <section class="section-shell split-section founder-story"><div class="portrait-placeholder large" aria-hidden="true"><span>AT</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Founder & owner</p><h2>Minister Altina Truss</h2><p>Altina Truss is an ordained minister, published author, poet, and entrepreneur. While pursuing theological studies, she discovered a deep call to help people through compassion, encouragement, and the daily practice of self-care.</p><p>Her vision is simple and expansive: create a nontraditional, welcoming space where people can experience Agape love—unconditional, intentional goodwill that seeks the best for others.</p></div></section>
  <section class="beliefs section-shell"><p class="eyebrow">What guides us</p><div class="belief-list"><p><span>01</span>Everyone deserves dignity, belonging, and care.</p><p><span>02</span>Rest and self-care can be purposeful, practical, and transformative.</p><p><span>03</span>Faith, love, and hope belong in everyday life.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
